<title>USA: Cort Business Services Q3 net rises.</title>
<headline>Cort Business Services Q3 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>FAIRFAX, Va. 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>CORT BUSINESS SERVICES CORPORATION</p>
<p>				RESULTS OF OPERATIONS</p>
<p>		   (in thousands, except per share amounts)</p>
<p>				Three Months Ended  Nine Months Ended</p>
<p>				     September 30,    September 30,</p>
<p>				   1996     1995	1996	 1995</p>
<p> Total revenue	     $64,607 $45,491   $171,484  $134,149</p>
<p> Costs and expenses(1)    54,577  38,598    146,077   114,579</p>
<p>    Operating earnings    10,030   6,893     25,407    19,570</p>
<p> Interest expense	    2,192   4,218	6,237    12,562</p>
<p> Income tax expense	  3,247   1,136	7,936     3,001</p>
<p> Net income		    4,591   1,539     11,234     4,007</p>
<p>Earnings per common</p>
<p>  share(2)			0.35    0.30	 0.93	0.80</p>
<p>Weighted average number</p>
<p>  of common shares	  12,976   7,242     12,075     7,241</p>
<p>PRO FORMA RESULTS - 1995(3)</p>
<p> Net income			 --   3,011	   --     8,365</p>
<p>  Earnings per common share   --    0.26	   --	0.72</p>
<p>(1) The 1996 nine month results include $425,000 of certain charges related to the 1996 Evans Rents acquisition.</p>
<p>(2) Earnings per common share for 1995 reflect the exchange of the Company's subordinated debt for equity as if it had occurred on January 1, 1994.</p>
<p>(3) Pro forma results reflect the impact of the Company's initial public offering and related debt retirement transactions as if they occurred at the beginning of the periods presented.  Therefore, pro forma net income excludes interest expense associated with the subordinated debt and $50 million of the senior notes.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
